# Adversarial evidence and review boundary

Run `python3 -B -m unittest tools.test_local_ci` from the trusted control checkout.
The suite creates disposable Git repositories and uses real Git objects, commits,
renames, deletions, source hashes and Linux namespace execution. It does not edit
canonical research. Workflow contract tests supplement actionlint; hosted execution
has not been measured under the account restriction.

| Failure/attack | Evidence in `tools/test_local_ci.py` | Required outcome |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Deleted/renamed source | `test_deleted_source`, `test_renamed_input_records_both_names` | Both rename endpoints retained; missing input prevents replay |
| Transitive helper outside package | `test_declared_outside_input_and_transitive_helper`, `test_undeclared_transitive_import` | Declared helper selects its dependent and replays; missing transitive input requires review |
| Undeclared package initializer | `test_undeclared_package_initializer` | Cannot substitute namespace-package behavior silently |
| Local package shadows standard library | `test_undeclared_package_shadowing_standard_library_requires_review`, `test_declared_package_shadowing_standard_library_is_replayed` | Missing local package initializer requires review; a declared initializer is replayed with its actual behavior |
| Dynamic import/filesystem input | `test_dynamic_import`, `test_undeclared_filesystem_input`, `test_dynamic_filesystem_input`, `test_declared_unresolved_input` | No closure claim or automatic replay |
| Shared/legacy certificate utility | `test_shared_certificate_utility`, `test_legacy_shared_helper_cannot_be_claimed_exclusive` | Comprehensive verification/review even if a new package declares the input |
| Canonical theorem/generated index | `test_canonical_theorem_change`, `test_state_generated_index_change` | Comprehensive verification/review; 94 certificates are not launched automatically |
| Generated package input | `test_declared_generated_input_selects_package`, `test_generated_input_missing_generator` | Select dependent; undeclared generator rejected |
| Unknown path/malformed metadata | `test_unknown_file`, `test_malformed_manifest`, `test_duplicate_json_keys` | Fail closed |
| Traversal/path aliases/symlinks | `test_traversal_aliases_and_special_paths`, `test_symlink` | Reject before materialization |
| Duplicate declarations | `test_duplicate_source`, `test_duplicate_identity` | Reject aliasing/hiding |
| Remove inputs/package edges | `test_removed_dependency_cannot_hide_changed_input`, `test_removing_package_edge_requires_review` | Old and new graph union prevents hidden impact; review required |
| Transitive/cyclic package graph | `test_package_edges_select_transitive_dependents`, `test_cyclic_package_edges` | Select transitive dependents; reject cycles |
| Missing/ambiguous ancestry | `test_missing_merge_base`, `test_real_criss_cross_ancestry`, `test_ambiguous_merge_base`, `test_shallow_history` | No range guess; review required |
| Target base advances after fork | `test_advanced_base_new_dependent_is_not_invisible`, `test_advanced_base_unrelated_package_does_not_expand_replay`, `test_advanced_base_changed_package_contract_needs_rebase` | Include new base dependents; require rebase for changed affected contracts; preserve unrelated locality |
| External inputs and legacy closure | `test_arbitrary_external_input_does_not_establish_legacy_closure` | Selection of a declared external input does not imply legacy closure |
| Force push/stale head/dirty files | `test_force_push_event`, `test_stale_pr_head`, `test_dirty_checkout` | No use of incomplete event or working tree |
| Forged serialized plan | `test_forged_plan_cannot_authorize_more_work` | Recompute authorization from exact Git endpoints |
| Workflow privilege/code attacks | `test_privileged_workflow_proposal_is_not_a_green_plan`, `test_malicious_privileged_import_is_rejected`, `test_workflow_permissions_and_gates` | Read-only tokens, trusted base tools, no privileged PR trigger, no candidate planner execution |
| Runtime sandbox escapes | `test_actual_namespace_hides_credentials_network_and_undeclared_files` | Host files, tokens, `.git`, network and writes to inputs unavailable |
| Optimization/false passing verifier | `test_replay_does_not_inherit_optimization_or_secrets` | Failing assertion remains failing despite inherited `PYTHONOPTIMIZE=2` |
| Timeout/unavailable sandbox | `test_timeout_fails_and_is_not_fully_verified`, `test_no_sandbox_means_no_replay` | Timeout or refusal; never a skipped success |
| Dependency installation/shell flags | `test_dependency_installation_is_not_silently_skipped`, `test_shell_and_interpreter_flags_rejected` | Unsupported dependency environment and command capabilities rejected |
| Reduced test domain | `test_new_domain_must_match_verify`, `test_coordinated_domain_reduction_requires_review`, `test_code_only_domain_reduction_cannot_report_full_verification` | Domain mismatch, coordinated contract reduction or loop reduction requires review; replay refused |
| Scanner fixtures / credential diagnostics | `test_scanner_fixture_is_not_a_private_key`, `test_whitespace_diagnostics_do_not_echo_credentials` | Literal test fixtures accepted; diagnostic text never echoes credential bytes |
| Oversized automatic workload | `test_workload_cap` | Two-package cap; no matrix expansion |

Every plan and scoped replay result has `full_verified: false`. Tests assert that
flag on fast, targeted, timeout, failure and comprehensive-review paths. The full
verifier is a different explicit operation. No fixture labels an unexecuted
required verifier as fully verified.

The domain tripwire is deliberately incomplete. No Python AST inspection can
prove that an arbitrary contributed verifier checks its claimed theorem. New
packages, data exclusions, early returns and obfuscated dynamic behavior still
need scientific review. Namespace execution binds the available input bytes; it
cannot prove that a verifier uses all of them correctly. A valid finite package
also cannot promote a global theorem. This distinction is retained in all JSON
outputs and contributor documentation.
